      "title": "PM to ask countries affected by UK’s role in slavery to help shape formal apology",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/02/andy-burnham-ask-countries-affected-uk-role-slavery-shape-formal-apology",
      "description": "<p>Andy Burnham to launch ‘structured dialogue’ on issue at Commonwealth summit in Antigua and Barbuda</p><p>Andy Burnham will ask countries affected by Britain’s role in slavery to help shape an expected formal apology, Downing Street has indicated, arguing that their input is indispensable in crafting an enduring message.</p><p>The prime minister was en route to the Commonwealth heads of government summit (Chogm) in Antigua and Barbuda, which begins on Tuesday. No 10 said he would use the event to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/01/uk-was-vehement-slavery-reparations-should-not-be-on-commonwealth-summit-agenda\">launch a “structured dialogue”</a> into what form an apology might take.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/02/andy-burnham-ask-countries-affected-uk-role-slavery-shape-formal-apology\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
